WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.580
This mundane house mouse

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.140
may hold clues to

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.520
when and how humans

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.120
first started farming

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.700
The question is: did people first settle down

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.180
you know, become sedentary

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.140
and then later start farming

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.940
or was farming the catalyst

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.760
that made people stay in one place?

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.400
So was it

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.460
hunter-gatherer, sedentism, and then farming

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.220
OR

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.960
hunter-gatherer, farming, and then sedentism

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.780
To figure this out, researchers looked at

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.640
the distribution of fossilized mouse teeth

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.440
From wild mice and house mice

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.960
They wanted to know when

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.340
house mice began dominating their wild cousins--

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.880
suggesting the house mice were living

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.880
close to humans

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.880
who had been there for a while,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.780
enjoying their shelters and leftovers

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.040
According to their results,

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.040
the house mouse

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.660
formed a beneficial relationship with people

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.940
15,000 years ago

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.980
This was before farming,

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.520
so that means people were

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.660
hunting and gathering in one place

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.440
long enough for house mice

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.440
to form a relationship with them

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.440
and out-compete their wild cousins

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.920
in the same location

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.440
So in this case is looks like it was

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.520
hunter-gatherer, sedentism, farming

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.540
NOT

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.380
hunter-gatherer, farming, then sedentism

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.800
As a side note:

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.260
It’s possible that this is why

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.960
you don’t see hunter-gatherers

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.120
domesticating cats

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.080
until after they transitioned to farming.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.280
Before there was grain for them to poach,

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.360
the mice weren’t considered pests,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.380
so no need to keep kitties around to control them.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.960
So looking at mouse teeth in different locations

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.080
may give us new insights into how this transition

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.140
to farming happened around the world

